{"id":"e2aafe50ba2f8c179c1c5065020e2db3468b2d94","axis":"silent","repo":"pnpm/pnpm","sha":"e2aafe50ba2f8c179c1c5065020e2db3468b2d94","parsed":{"files":[{"path":".changeset/pnpr-release-record-logs.md","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,5 @@","+---","+\"@pnpm/pnpr\": minor","+---","+","+pnpr logs the release records of the npm versions it hosts with SQLite or libSQL metadata. Each hosted organization has a transparency log per ecosystem, in the C2SP tiled log format. A version's log entry is recorded in the same transaction that accepts the version. With `releaseRecords.logSigningKey` set, pnpr then adds the entry to the log's tiles and signs a new checkpoint, keeping both in the hosted store. The metadata database's schema changed, so a database written by an earlier pnpr is refused."],"additions":5,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"Cargo.lock","lines":["@@ -7000,6 +7000,7 @@ dependencies = [","  \"pnpm-store-dir\",","  \"pnpm-tarball\",","  \"pnpm-testing-utils\",","+ \"pnpm-transparency-log\",","  \"pnpr-auth\",","  \"pnpr-cargo\",","  \"pnpr-config\",","@@ -7101,6 +7102,7 @@ dependencies = [","  \"pnpm-config-dir\",","  \"pnpm-env-replace\",","  \"pnpm-testing-utils\",","+ \"pnpm-transparency-log\",","  \"pnpr-error\",","  \"pnpr-package-name\",","  \"pnpr-policy\",","@@ -7332,6 +7334,7 @@ dependencies = [","  \"pnpm-network\",","  \"pnpm-package-manifest\",","  \"pnpm-release-record\",","+ \"pnpm-transparency-log\",","  \"pnpr-config\",","  \"pnpr-error\",","  \"pnpr-libsql\",","@@ -7343,6 +7346,7 @@ dependencies = [","  \"serde_json\",","  \"ssri\",","  \"tempfile\",","+ \"tlog_tiles\",","  \"tokio\",","  \"tracing\","," ]"],"additions":4,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"pnpm/crates/transparency-log/src/keys/signer.rs","lines":["@@ -37,6 +37,12 @@ impl NoteSigner {","         Ok(signer)","     }"," ","+    /// A signer with the same Ed25519 key under another name, such as one","+    /// log of a registry that names each log's checkpoint key after it.","+    pub fn renamed(&self, name: &str) -> Result<Self, KeyError> {","+        NoteSigner::new(name, self.signing_key.clone())","+    }","+","     /// The key that verifies this signer's signatures.","     #[must_use]","     pub const fn verifier_key(&self) -> &VerifierKey {"],"additions":6,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"pnpm/crates/transparency-log/src/keys/tests.rs","lines":["@@ -121,3 +121,22 @@ fn rejects_invalid_names() {","     }","     VerifierKey::new(&\"n\".repeat(255), KeyAlgorithm::CosignatureV1, public_key).unwrap();"," }","+","+#[test]","+fn a_renamed_signer_keeps_its_key_under_the_new_name() {","+    let signer = NoteSigner::from_private_key(PETER_PRIVATE_KEY).unwrap();","+    let renamed = signer.renamed(\"registry.example/npm\").unwrap();","+    assert_eq!(renamed.verifier_key().name(), \"registry.example/npm\");","+    assert_eq!(","+        renamed","+            .verifier_key()","+            .public_key()","+            .to_bytes(),","+        signer","+            .verifier_key()","+            .public_key()","+            .to_bytes(),","+    );","+    assert_ne!(renamed.verifier_key().key_id(), signer.verifier_key().key_id());","+    assert!(signer.renamed(\"two words\").is_err());","+}"],"additions":19,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"pnpr/crates/config/Cargo.toml","lines":["@@ -17,6 +17,7 @@ pnpr-policy = { workspace = true }"," pnpr-registry = { workspace = true }"," pnpm-config-dir = { workspace = true }"," pnpm-env-replace = { workspace = true }","+pnpm-transparency-log = { workspace = true }"," getrandom = { workspace = true }"," home = { workspace = true }"," indexmap = { workspace = true }"],"additions":1,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"pnpr/crates/config/src/config_file.rs","lines":["@@ -1,7 +1,8 @@"," use super::{","     AccessSpec, ByteSize, Deserialize, Ecosystem, IndexMap, Interval, LogConfig, LogFormat,","     LogLevel, Management, MetricsConfig, OciConfig, PackageAccess, PackageDocumentsFile, PathBuf,","-    S3Settings, ScimConfig, TarballFormat, UpstreamAuthFile, default_storage_string, oidc,","+    ReleaseRecordsFile, S3Settings, ScimConfig, TarballFormat, UpstreamAuthFile,","+    default_storage_string, oidc,"," };"," "," /// Disk shape of the `routes:` block.","@@ -223,6 +224,9 @@ pub(super) struct ConfigFile {","     /// pnpr-only: how pnpr's own package document is served.","     #[serde(default)]","     pub(super) package_documents: Option<PackageDocumentsFile>,","+    /// pnpr-only: how the release records of hosted versions are logged.","+    #[serde(default)]","+    pub(super) release_records: Option<ReleaseRecordsFile>,","     /// pnpr-only browser access policy. Cross-origin access stays disabled","     /// when this block is absent or its allowlist is empty.","     #[serde(default)]"],"additions":5,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"pnpr/crates/config/src/lib.rs","lines":["@@ -18,6 +18,7 @@ pub use logging::{LogConfig, LogFormat, LogLevel};"," pub use metrics::MetricsConfig;"," pub use package_documents::PackageDocumentsConfig;"," pub use pnpr_policy::{TeamDirectory, Teams};","+pub use release_records::ReleaseRecordsConfig;"," pub use s3::{HostedStoreConfig, S3Settings, build_s3_store, normalize_key_prefix};"," pub use scim::ScimConfig;"," pub use secrets::{MIN_RESOLUTION_SECRET_LEN, derive_subkey, random_secret, resolution_secret};","@@ -61,6 +62,8 @@ mod metrics;"," "," mod package_documents;"," use package_documents::{PackageDocumentsFile, build_package_documents_config};","+mod release_records;","+use release_records::{ReleaseRecordsFile, build_release_records_config};"," "," mod registry_graph;"," use registry_graph::{","@@ -161,6 +164,8 @@ pub struct Config {","     pub identity: IdentityConfig,","     pub features: Features,","     pub routing: RoutingConfig,","+    /// How the release records of hosted versions are logged.","+    pub release_records: ReleaseRecordsConfig,"," }"," "," impl std::fmt::Debug for Config {","@@ -177,6 +182,7 @@ impl std::fmt::Debug for Config {","             .field(\"identity\", &self.identity)","             .field(\"features\", &self.features)","             .field(\"routing\", &self.routing)","+            .field(\"release_records\", &self.release_records)","             .finish()","     }"," }"],"additions":6,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"pnpr/crates/config/src/loading.rs","lines":["@@ -243,6 +243,7 @@ impl Config {","             identity: build_identity_config(&file.auth, base_dir, backend)?,","             features,","             routing,","+            release_records: super::build_release_records_config(file.release_records.take())?,","         })","     }"," }"],"additions":1,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"pnpr/crates/config/src/release_records.rs","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,55 @@","+use super::{Deserialize, RegistryError};","+use pnpm_transparency_log::NoteSigner;","+use std::{fmt, sync::Arc};","+","+/// How pnpr logs the release records of the versions it hosts","+/// ([release records](https://github.com/pnpm/rfcs/blob/92d2b281af321ecf8f1e5fea63f698716ba4e9e7/pnpr/text/0000-release-records.md)).","+///","+/// Every record's log entry is sequenced when its version is accepted,","+/// whether or not a key is configured. With a key, pnpr integrates the","+/// sequenced entries into each log's tiles and signs its checkpoints.","+#[derive(Default, Clone)]","+pub struct ReleaseRecordsConfig {","+    /// The key that signs every log's checkpoints. Its name is the name","+    /// every log's origin starts with, and each log signs under its own","+    /// origin with the same Ed25519 key. `None` publishes no logs.","+    pub log_signing_key: Option<Arc<NoteSigner>>,","+}","+","+impl fmt::Debug for ReleaseRecordsConfig {","+    fn fmt(&self, formatter: &mut fmt::Formatter<'_>) -> fmt::Result {","+        let key = self.log_signing_key","+            .as_ref()","+            .map(|signer| signer.verifier_key().to_string());","+        formatter","+            .debug_struct(\"ReleaseRecordsConfig\")","+            .field(\"log_signing_key\", &key)","+            .finish()","+    }","+}","+","+/// Disk shape of the `releaseRecords:` block.","+#[derive(Debug, Default, Deserialize)]","+#[serde(rename_all = \"camelCase\", deny_unknown_fields)]","+pub(super) struct ReleaseRecordsFile {","+    /// A signed-note private key, `PRIVATE+KEY+<name>+<key hash>+<key>`, as","+    /// Go's `note.GenerateKey` writes one.","+    #[serde(default)]","+    log_signing_key: Option<String>,","+}","+","+pub(super) fn build_release_records_config(","+    file: Option<ReleaseRecordsFile>,","+) -> Result<ReleaseRecordsConfig, RegistryError> {","+    let Some(key) = file.and_then(|file| file.log_signing_key) else {","+        return Ok(ReleaseRecordsConfig::default());","+    };","+    let signer = NoteSigner::from_private_key(key.trim()).map_err(|err| {","+        RegistryError::InvalidConfig {","+            reason: format!(","+                \"releaseRecords.logSigningKey is not a PRIVATE+KEY+<name>+<hash>+<key> signed-note key: {err}\",","+            ),","+        }","+    })?;","+    Ok(ReleaseRecordsConfig { log_signing_key: Some(Arc::new(signer)) })","+}"],"additions":55,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"pnpr/crates/config/src/secrets.rs","lines":["@@ -123,6 +123,19 @@ fn validate_root_secrets<Sys: EnvVar>(val: &serde_json::Value) -> Result<(), Reg","     Ok(())"," }"," ","+fn validate_release_record_secrets<Sys: EnvVar>(","+    val: &serde_json::Value,","+) -> Result<(), RegistryError> {","+    let key = val","+        .get(\"releaseRecords\")","+        .and_then(|records| records.get(\"logSigningKey\"))","+        .and_then(serde_json::Value::as_str);","+    match key {","+        Some(key) => check_secret_env_field::<Sys>(\"releaseRecords.logSigningKey\", key),","+        None => Ok(()),","+    }","+}","+"," fn validate_s3_secrets<Sys: EnvVar>(val: &serde_json::Value) -> Result<(), RegistryError> {","     let Some(s3) = val.get(\"s3\").and_then(serde_json::Value::as_object) else {","         return Ok(());","@@ -243,6 +256,7 @@ pub(crate) fn validate_secret_env_vars<Sys: EnvVar>(raw: &str) -> Result<(), Reg","         return Ok(());","     };","     validate_root_secrets::<Sys>(&val)?;","+    validate_release_record_secrets::<Sys>(&val)?;","     validate_s3_secrets::<Sys>(&val)?;","     validate_auth_secrets::<Sys>(&val)?;","     validate_database_secrets::<Sys>(&val)?;"],"additions":14,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"pnpr/crates/config/src/tests/server_options.rs","lines":["@@ -451,3 +451,29 @@ fn package_documents_reject_a_window_shorter_than_30_days() {","         assert!(matches!(result, Err(RegistryError::InvalidConfig { .. })), \"accepted {yaml:?}\");","     }"," }","+","+/// Go's `note` test key, as `note.GenerateKey` writes it.","+const LOG_SIGNING_KEY: &str =","+    \"PRIVATE+KEY+PeterNeumann+c74f20a3+AYEKFALVFGyNhPJEMzD1QIDr+Y7hfZx09iUvxdXHKDFz\";","+","+#[test]","+fn release_records_publish_no_logs_without_a_signing_key() {","+    let config = Config::from_yaml_str(\"\", Path::new(\"/config\"), listen(), None).unwrap();","+    assert!(config.release_records.log_signing_key.is_none());","+}","+","+#[test]","+fn release_records_read_the_log_signing_key() {","+    let yaml = format!(\"releaseRecords:\\n  logSigningKey: {LOG_SIGNING_KEY}\\n\");","+    let config = Config::from_yaml_str(&yaml, Path::new(\"/config\"), listen(), None).unwrap();","+    let signer = config.release_records.log_signing_key.clone().unwrap();","+    assert_eq!(signer.verifier_key().key_name(), \"PeterNeumann+c74f20a3\");","+    assert!(!format!(\"{:?}\", config.release_records).contains(\"AYEKFALV\"));","+","+    let mangled = format!(\"releaseRecords:\\n  logSigningKey: {}x\\n\", &LOG_SIGNING_KEY[..60]);","+    let err = Config::from_yaml_str(&mangled, Path::new(\"/config\"), listen(), None).unwrap_err();","+    assert!(","+        matches!(err, RegistryError::InvalidConfig { ref reason } if reason.contains(\"logSigningKey\")),","+        \"{err:?}\",","+    );","+}"],"additions":26,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"pnpr/crates/pnpr-fixtures/src/presets.rs","lines":["@@ -227,5 +227,6 @@ fn with_routing(","             pipeline: PipelineFeature::default(),","         },","         routing,","+        release_records: pnpr_config::ReleaseRecordsConfig::default(),","     }"," }"],"additions":1,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"pnpr/crates/pnpr/Cargo.toml","lines":["@@ -70,6 +70,7 @@ pnpm-store-dir = { workspace = true }"," pnpm-shared-artifact-protocol = { workspace = true }"," pnpm-platform-variants = { workspace = true }"," pnpm-release-record = { workspace = true }","+pnpm-transparency-log = { workspace = true }"," pnpm-tarball = { workspace = true }"," async-trait = { workspace = true }"," axum = { workspace = true, features = [\"query\"] }"],"additions":1,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"pnpr/crates/pnpr/src/server.rs","lines":["@@ -9,6 +9,7 @@ pub(crate) use tcp_listener::PeerAddr;"," pub(crate) use self::striped_locks::StripedLocks;"," "," mod lifecycle;","+mod release_record_logs;"," use lifecycle::load_active_osv_index;"," "," mod tcp_listener;"],"additions":1,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"pnpr/crates/pnpr/src/server/publishing/atomic.rs","lines":["@@ -24,6 +24,7 @@ use pnpr_storage::{","         ArtifactMember, BatchDocument, Generation, PublicationCommit, PublicationRequest,","         PublishNotes,","     },","+    transparency_log::LogId,"," };"," use serde_json::json;"," use ssri::{Algorithm, IntegrityOpts};","@@ -169,6 +170,34 @@ async fn commit_staged(","     };","     let promoted = promote_archives(state, &mut staged).await?;","     let artifacts = promoted.artifacts.clone();","+    let (documents, logged) = batch_documents(staged);","+    let commit =","+        match database.commit_publication(&catalog, documents, artifacts, notes, request).await {","+            Ok(commit) => commit,","+            Err(err) => {","+                promoted.remove_written(state).await;","+                return Err(err);","+            }","+        };","+    if !commit.replayed {","+        for ecosystem in logged {","+            let log = LogId { catalog: catalog.clone(), ecosystem };","+            super::super::release_record_logs::integrate_in_background(state, log);","+        }","+    }","+    Ok(commit.into())","+}","+","+/// The documents a commit writes, and the ecosystems whose logs the records","+/// they bring are sequenced in.","+fn batch_documents(","+    staged: Vec<StagedPublish>,","+) -> (Vec<BatchDocument>, std::collections::BTreeSet<pnpr_package_name::Ecosystem>) {","+    let logged = staged","+        .iter()","+        .filter(|stage| !stage.verification.records.is_empty())","+        .map(|stage| stage.ecosystem)","+        .collect();","     let documents = staged","         .into_iter()","         .map(|stage| BatchDocument {","@@ -180,15 +209,7 @@ async fn commit_staged(","             records: stage.verification.records,","         })","         .collect();","-    let commit =","-        match database.commit_publication(&catalog, documents, artifacts, notes, request).await {","-            Ok(commit) => commit,","-            Err(err) => {","-                promoted.remove_written(state).await;","-                return Err(err);","-            }","-        };","-    Ok(commit.into())","+    (documents, logged)"," }"," "," /// The one organization every package of a publish belongs to. A"],"additions":30,"deletions":9,"truncated":false},{"path":"pnpr/crates/pnpr/src/server/release_record_logs.rs","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,102 @@","+//! Integrating the transparency logs of hosted release records","+//! ([release records](https://github.com/pnpm/rfcs/blob/92d2b281af321ecf8f1e5fea63f698716ba4e9e7/pnpr/text/0000-release-records.md#transparency-log)).","+//!","+//! A record's log entry is sequenced when its version is accepted. A commit","+//! that sequenced entries integrates their log in the background, and each","+//! server once integrates every log, which picks up whatever an interrupted","+//! integration left: when its router is built, or, for a router built","+//! outside a Tokio runtime, at the first integration it starts. A publication's success means committed, not yet","+//! integrated. Without a log signing key, entries are sequenced and nothing","+//! is integrated.","+","+use super::AppState;","+use pnpr_storage::transparency_log::LogId;","+use std::sync::{Arc, atomic::Ordering};","+","+/// Integrate `log` in the background, after a commit that sequenced entries","+/// into it.","+pub(super) fn integrate_in_background(state: &AppState, log: LogId) {","+    let Some(key) = state.inner.config.release_records.log_signing_key.clone() else {","+        return;","+    };","+    integrate_sequenced_logs(state);","+    let state = state.clone();","+    tokio::spawn(async move {","+        let _integrating = state.inner.locks.log_integration.lock().await;","+        if let Err(error) = state.inner.storage.integrate_log(&log, &key).await {","+            tracing::warn!(%error, %log, \"integrating a transparency log failed\");","+            // The next trigger scans every log again, this one included.","+            state.inner.locks.logs_recovered.store(false, Ordering::Release);","+        }","+    });","+}","+","+/// Integrate, in the background, every log whose entries were sequenced,","+/// once per server, as after an unclean shutdown. Outside a Tokio runtime it","+/// does nothing and leaves the scan to the next call. It shares the server's","+/// storage and its integration lock with the integrations commits start, so","+/// one process never integrates a log twice at once: the filesystem","+/// backend's compare-and-set of a checkpoint holds only within one store.","+pub(super) fn integrate_sequenced_logs(state: &AppState) {","+    let Some(key) = state.inner.config.release_records.log_signing_key.clone() else {","+        return;","+    };","+    let storage = state.inner.storage.clone();","+    let Some(database) = storage.sql_metadata().cloned() else { return };","+    let Ok(runtime) = tokio::runtime::Handle::try_current() else { return };","+    if state.inner.locks.logs_recovered.swap(true, Ordering::AcqRel) {","+        return;","+    }","+    // A scan that fails or never finishes, because its runtime shut down,","+    // is retried by the next call.","+    let mut retry = RetryRecovery(Some(state.clone()));","+    let lock = Arc::clone(&state.inner.locks.log_integration);","+    runtime.spawn(async move {","+        let _integrating = lock.lock().await;","+        if integrate_every_log(&storage, &database, &key).await {","+            retry.disarm();","+        }","+    });","+}","+","+/// Clears a server's `logs_recovered` when dropped holding it, so a","+/// recovery scan that failed or was cancelled runs again.","+struct RetryRecovery(Option<AppState>);","+","+impl RetryRecovery {","+    /// Keep `logs_recovered` set: the scan succeeded.","+    fn disarm(&mut self) {","+        self.0 = None;","+    }","+}","+","+impl Drop for RetryRecovery {","+    fn drop(&mut self) {","+        if let Some(state) = &self.0 {","+            state.inner.locks.logs_recovered.store(false, Ordering::Release);","+        }","+    }","+}","+","+/// Integrate every sequenced log, reporting whether all of them were.","+async fn integrate_every_log(","+    storage: &pnpr_storage::Storage,","+    database: &Arc<pnpr_storage::metadata::SqlMetadata>,","+    key: &pnpm_transparency_log::NoteSigner,","+) -> bool {","+    let logs = match database.sequenced_logs().await {","+        Ok(logs) => logs,","+        Err(error) => {","+            tracing::warn!(%error, \"listing the transparency logs to integrate failed\");","+            return false;","+        }","+    };","+    let mut integrated = true;","+    for (log, _) in logs {","+        if let Err(error) = storage.integrate_log(&log, key).await {","+            tracing::warn!(%error, %log, \"integrating a transparency log failed\");","+            integrated = false;","+        }","+    }","+    integrated","+}"],"additions":102,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"pnpr/crates/pnpr/src/server/routing.rs","lines":["@@ -80,6 +80,9 @@ pub(super) fn state_and_router(","     let ui_dir = if surfaces.registry { super::web_ui::locate(&config.http.ui)? } else { None };","     let state = AppState { inner: Arc::new(AppInner::new(config, auth, osv_index)?) };","     let router = finish_router(state.clone(), surfaces, cors_origins, ui_dir.as_deref())?;","+    // Every router, also one an embedder builds directly, picks up what an","+    // interrupted integration of the release record logs left.","+    super::release_record_logs::integrate_sequenced_logs(&state);","     Ok((state, router))"," }"," "],"additions":3,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"pnpr/crates/pnpr/src/server/state.rs","lines":["@@ -69,6 +69,11 @@ pub(super) struct MutationLocks {","     /// The same, per principal, so one account cannot hold every upload","     /// permit. See [`super::staged_archives::PrincipalUploads`].","     pub(super) staged_archive_uploads_by_principal: super::staged_archives::PrincipalUploads,","+    /// Held while this instance integrates a transparency log, so its","+    /// integrations run one at a time.","+    pub(super) log_integration: Arc<tokio::sync::Mutex<()>>,","+    /// Set once this server started integrating every sequenced log.","+    pub(super) logs_recovered: std::sync::atomic::AtomicBool,"," }"," "," pub(super) struct IdentityServices {","@@ -106,6 +111,8 @@ impl AppInner {","                 ),","                 staged_archive_uploads_by_principal:","                     super::staged_archives::PrincipalUploads::default(),","+                log_integration: Arc::new(tokio::sync::Mutex::new(())),","+                logs_recovered: std::sync::atomic::AtomicBool::new(false),","             },","             identity,","             metrics: Arc::new(ServerMetrics::new()),"],"additions":7,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"pnpr/crates/pnpr/tests/sql_metadata.rs","lines":["@@ -339,6 +339,90 @@ async fn a_version_is_accepted_with_its_release_record() {","     assert_eq!(again, bytes);"," }"," ","+/// Go's `note` test key.","+const LOG_SIGNING_KEY: &str =","+    \"PRIVATE+KEY+PeterNeumann+c74f20a3+AYEKFALVFGyNhPJEMzD1QIDr+Y7hfZx09iUvxdXHKDFz\";","+","+/// A publish sequences the record's log entry, and pnpr integrates it into","+/// the log's tiles and a signed checkpoint after the commit.","+#[tokio::test]","+async fn a_published_record_is_integrated_into_its_log() {","+    let tmp = TempDir::new().unwrap();","+    let mut config = sqlite_config(tmp.path());","+    let signer = pnpm_transparency_log::NoteSigner::from_private_key(LOG_SIGNING_KEY).unwrap();","+    config.release_records.log_signing_key = Some(std::sync::Arc::new(signer));","+    let storage = pnpr_storage::Storage::from_config(&config.storage).unwrap();","+    let app = router(config);","+    let token = token(&app).await;","+    let (_, tgz) = crate::server::package_tar_and_tgz(r#\"{\"name\":\"logged\",\"version\":\"1.0.0\"}\"#);","+    let doc = publish_doc(\"logged\", \"1.0.0\", &tgz);","+    let (status, ..) = send(&app, request(\"PUT\", \"/npm/logged\", &token, Some(&doc))).await;","+    assert_eq!(status, StatusCode::CREATED);","+","+    let database = storage.sql_metadata().unwrap();","+    let logs = database.sequenced_logs().await.unwrap();","+    let [(log, 1)] = logs.as_slice() else { panic!(\"{logs:?}\") };","+    let deadline = std::time::Instant::now() + std::time::Duration::from_secs(10);","+    let checkpoint = loop {","+        if let Some(checkpoint) = storage.log_checkpoint(log).await.unwrap() {","+            break checkpoint;","+        }","+        assert!(std::time::Instant::now() < deadline, \"the log was never integrated\");","+        tokio::time::sleep(std::time::Duration::from_millis(20)).await;","+    };","+    assert_eq!(checkpoint.tree_head.size, 1);","+    assert!(checkpoint.tree_head.origin.starts_with(\"PeterNeumann/npm\"), \"{checkpoint:?}\");","+    let entries = database","+        .log_entries(log, 0..1)","+        .await","+        .unwrap();","+    let entry = pnpm_release_record::LogEntry::parse(&entries[0]).unwrap();","+    assert_eq!(entry.key().subject_name(), \"pkg:npm/logged@1.0.0\");","+}","+","+/// A router integrates what was sequenced before it was built, such as the","+/// entries of a registry that had no log signing key yet.","+#[tokio::test]","+async fn a_new_router_integrates_what_was_sequenced_before() {","+    let tmp = TempDir::new().unwrap();","+    let unsigned = router(sqlite_config(tmp.path()));","+    let token = token(&unsigned).await;","+    let (_, tgz) = crate::server::package_tar_and_tgz(r#\"{\"name\":\"early\",\"version\":\"1.0.0\"}\"#);","+    let doc = publish_doc(\"early\", \"1.0.0\", &tgz);","+    let (status, ..) = send(&unsigned, request(\"PUT\", \"/npm/early\", &token, Some(&doc))).await;","+    assert_eq!(status, StatusCode::CREATED);","+    let storage = pnpr_storage::Storage::from_config(&sqlite_config(tmp.path()).storage).unwrap();","+    let logs = storage","+        .sql_metadata()","+        .unwrap()","+        .sequenced_logs()","+        .await","+        .unwrap();","+    let [(log, 1)] = logs.as_slice() else { panic!(\"{logs:?}\") };","+    assert!(","+        storage","+            .log_checkpoint(log)","+            .await","+            .unwrap()","+            .is_none(),","+    );","+","+    let mut config = sqlite_config(tmp.path());","+    let signer = pnpm_transparency_log::NoteSigner::from_private_key(LOG_SIGNING_KEY).unwrap();","+    config.release_records.log_signing_key = Some(std::sync::Arc::new(signer));","+    let _signed = router(config);","+    let deadline = std::time::Instant::now() + std::time::Duration::from_secs(10);","+    while storage","+        .log_checkpoint(log)","+        .await","+        .unwrap()","+        .is_none()","+    {","+        assert!(std::time::Instant::now() < deadline, \"the new router integrated nothing\");","+        tokio::time::sleep(std::time::Duration::from_millis(20)).await;","+    }","+}","+"," async fn get_json_document(app: &Router, path: &str, token: &str) -> (StatusCode, Value) {","     let (status, _, body) = send(app, request(\"GET\", path, token, None)).await;","     (status, serde_json::from_slice(&body).unwrap())"],"additions":84,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"pnpr/crates/storage/Cargo.toml","lines":["@@ -23,6 +23,7 @@ pnpr-registry = { workspace = true }"," pnpm-crypto-hash = { workspace = true }"," pnpm-package-manifest = { workspace = true }"," pnpm-release-record = { workspace = true }","+pnpm-transparency-log = { workspace = true }"," async-trait = { workspace = true }"," axum = { workspace = true }"," base64 = { workspace = true }","@@ -37,6 +38,7 @@ serde = { workspace = true }"," serde_json = { workspace = true }"," ssri = { workspace = true }"," tokio = { workspace = true }","+tlog_tiles = { workspace = true }"," tempfile = { workspace = true }"," tracing = { workspace = true }"," ","@@ -48,6 +50,7 @@ pnpr-libsql = { workspace = true, features = [\"testing\"] }"," reqwest = { workspace = true }"," tempfile = { workspace = true }"," tokio = { workspace = true }","+tlog_tiles = { workspace = true }"," "," [target.'cfg(not(target_family = \"wasm\"))'.dependencies]"," tokio = { workspace = true, features = [\"net\", \"signal\"] }"],"additions":3,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"pnpr/crates/storage/src/lib.rs","lines":["@@ -9,6 +9,7 @@ pub mod publish;"," pub mod streaming;"," "," pub mod tombstones;","+pub mod transparency_log;"," "," pub mod upload;"," "],"additions":1,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"pnpr/crates/storage/src/metadata/sql.rs","lines":["@@ -39,6 +39,7 @@ mod cache;"," mod commit;"," #[cfg